    Bug 1928032 - Improve pagination mechanism and rework tests. r=edicharry


    To resolve the intermittent pagination fails, the mechanism is improved and the
    tests are reworked using a different approach.

    * A new page is now added as soon as the pagination timeout is reached.
      Before: After a message had been added to the page and the timeout had not
      yet been reached, the next message was processed. If that message, however,
      massively exceeded the timeout, the page was only returned after that message
      had been added.
      Now : The page is already created while the second message is still being
      processed, returning the page shortly after the timeout has elapsed.

    * Since we do not actually test different protocol implementations, the
      XPCSHELL pagination tests have been converted to browser tests.

    * The tests no longer create custom Experiments to test derived API classes,
      but instead access the global `MessageListTracker` instances used by all
      extensions and mock certain methods of the actual API implementation.

    * The `MessageListTracker` class can now be mocked in automation to provide
      better control over page and message additions, preventing intermittent
      timing issues.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D283604

